WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Good morning, John!

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.580
We are fast approaching the ninety-eighth birthday of one my favorite people

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.400
in the world, though he may be dead: Alan Turing.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.180
Now, Alan is one of my favorite people because:

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.880
1) He was a colossal nerd; and

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.840
2) He helped win World War II;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.880
and 3) He helped create the machine that you are staring at right now!

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.900
And John, I love the machine you are staring at right now.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.640
I love it...a lot.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.360
And not only was he making them, but he was programming to make codes

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.080
for the English military and to break the codes of the German military!

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.220
Yes, Alan Turing is responsible for many of the amazing things that we enjoy today,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.300
things that may or may not include not living in a world governed by radical, totalitarian, antisemitic jerks;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.780
and also may include not living in a world where I am a professional vlogger.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.680
I don't even know which one of those things would be worse.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.060
But while Alan Turing did a lot of amazing things for the world, in particularly for the British government,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.940
the British government did not do a great job paying him back for that.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.080
In the 1950s, Alan Turing was convicted of being a homosexual,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.360
which does not to us sound like a thing you can be convicted of.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.020
But yes! He went to court and there was a jury

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.840
and they convicted him of being a homosexual.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.600
Indeed, it was illegal in England in the 1950s

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.460
to be gay.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.840
And Oscar Wilde was actually convicted with the exact same law.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.880
Oscar Wilde was sentenced to two years, hard labor

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.200
for being a homosexual.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.540
Alan Turing got to choose between his punishments:

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.120
either two years in jail

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.560
or 2) undergo hormonal treatment

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.220
to decrease his libido.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.740
Alan Turing chose the second choice

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.920
and took the estrogen hormonal injections.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.520
After his conviction his security clearance was revoked,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.220
he was not allowed to work on any of the computers he had developed,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.300
his name was tarnished, and there were implications that homosexuals

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.880
were often spies.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.140
Soon after, in 1954, Alan Turing injected an apple with cyanide

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.220
and then he ate it.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.100
Alan Turing did everything that a person can do

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.980
to win the support of his nation.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.900
Everything! He saved thousands, possibly hundreds of

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.960
thousands of the lives of British soldiers.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.580
He created machines that would go on to revolutionize the entire world,

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.060
but because there was one thing

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.600
that was a little bit different about him

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.600
his entire country turned their back on him.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.400
I'm telling you this story because I want to think about change.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.920
This week, The Trevor Project is working on a video contest called

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.380
"Be The Change".

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.380
And sometimes it's hard to see change.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.100
It's hard to see change happening,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.960
especially for young people. Like, I feel like

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:14.940
if you're 15-years-old

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:19.220
you can't see how fast the world has changed.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.120
Because, really, since you started paying attention,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.580
when you were 10 maybe,

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.220
the world hasn't changed that much, so

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.760
it might seem like nothing can ever change.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.260
And that's when people get desperate.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.940
And they things like complete suicide because they

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.500
happen to be lesbians, or gay, or bisexual, or transgendered, or questioning,

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.720
but if you think about Alan Turing, then you can realize

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.400
that so much has changed!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.820
And yes, there's a lot of change still to make!

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.260
But that doesn't happen all at once.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.980
There's never a moment where everyone just agrees to be tolerant.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.100
It happens slowly. It happens very slowly.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.360
And it happens through a lot of different mechanisms,

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.080
but the most important one is to change yourself.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.540
If enough of us change then the change happens.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.820
And that's what's happened.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.200
That is why you can no longer go to jail for being a homosexual:

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.120
because people changed, individual people.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.460
And how can you be the change? Well,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.240
you can support The Trevor Project,

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.920
you can go to memelabs.com/trevorproject/ and watch

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.920
a bunch of these videos and vote on your favorites,

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.920
or you can make your own Be The Change video.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.240
And I hope that you do.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.480
John, I will see you on Wednesday.

